From c4f5d939dc8318285db7fc73cf3e4313148a9377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 19:22:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] riscv: mm: map the kernel into swapper_pg_dir on 32-bit
 XIP

setup_vm_final() only installs the kernel mapping into swapper_pg_dir
on 64-bit, relying on the linear mapping to cover the kernel on 32-bit.
That assumption breaks on XIP: the flash-resident text lives outside
RAM and is not part of the linear mapping, so the first instruction
fetch after switching satp to swapper_pg_dir faults, with the trap
vector itself unmapped, wedging the machine in a fault loop.

Call create_kernel_page_table() on XIP as well. Its XIP variant maps
the text from kernel_map.xiprom and the data from RAM, and is already
used to populate early_pg_dir.

Co-developed-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/riscv/mm/init.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/mm/init.c b/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
index 5c9e18467..486ad0ece 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/mm/init.c
@@ -1358,8 +1358,12 @@ static void __init setup_vm_final(void)
 	/* Map the linear mapping */
 	create_linear_mapping_page_table();
 
-	/* Map the kernel */
-	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_64BIT))
+	/*
+	 * Map the kernel: on 64-bit the kernel lives outside the linear
+	 * mapping, and on XIP the flash-resident text is not covered by the
+	 * linear mapping either (only the data copy in RAM is).
+	 */
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_64BIT) || IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_XIP_KERNEL))
 		create_kernel_page_table(swapper_pg_dir, false);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_KASAN
